{'name': "Petrini's Restaurant", 'address': '5711 Calle Real', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'American (New), Italian, Restaurants, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '16:30-21:0', 'Tuesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Wednesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '16:30-21:0', 'Friday': '16:30-21:30', 'Saturday': '16:30-21:0', 'Sunday': '16:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2016-09-02 07:51:10', 'review_text': "I tend not to expect much from food locations in Strip Malls.  While staying in the Santa Barbara area, I just wanted a good piece of Pizza. We stopped here while on a walk and ordered an onion and cheese pizza, small size.  Neither of us could believe how fresh and great it was! The sauce was a good homemade red with Italian spices and fresh tomato flavor. Just enough good cheese.  We stopped in twice after having such great luck.  Tried the salads, pasta and more pizza, garlic bread and wine.  Family owned and run place that's cordial and homey.   This is the kind of place you find in Chicago and New York. Just a little gem with friendly people and really good Italian food!"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2016-08-17 01:35:09', 'review_text': "Well, I tried eating at this Petrini's again, and I'm really sad to report that the food has gotten worse AND more expensive. The Chicken Picatta was drowning in butter, or grease; I'm not sure what that was. The fettuccine Alfredo that came with it was undercooked and had zero taste. We also were served garlic bread that was burned to black. To make things worse, I took the food home because I just could eat it at the restaurant. I was hungry later so I ate it. 
Oh My God.....I couldn't keep it down. I got such a stomach ache from that food. Petrini's , you are a local restaurant and I really try to support local businesses, but you are bad for my health."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2016-07-11 15:51:04', 'review_text': 'I have not been in here for many years, but we stopped in the other night and it was tasty traditional american italian food for a great price. The meat raviolis were very tender and delicious and the sauce was spot on. The spaghetti and meatballs (the yard stick for any italian review) were also very good. I also really enjoyed my cup of minestrone soup, really hit the spot. The waiters were very attentive and the place had a very welcoming and tidy atmosphere. 

The only downside, the water tasted horrible, I think they need to replace their filter or something.'}]}

{'name': 'Piranha Restaurant & Sushi Bar', 'address': '714 State St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Sushi Bars', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-08-08 19:51:46', 'review_text': 'The sushi was mediocre but I still like the environment and the service!'}, {'review_stars': 2.0, 'review_date': '2008-07-26 05:03:21', 'review_text': '"after a lovely day at the beach, my husband and i decided to finish off the day with some sushi. we'd eaten at piranha before and enjoyed it, but after tonight's experience, i can safely say we will never return. it wasn't heinous--but for 80$, the quality of the food and service was pretty abysmal. not only was the sushi NOT super fresh and tasty, especially as compared to katsuya in encino, but the waitstaff was inattentive (we had to call out for the hostess finally to get our waitress's attention), the waitress made a mistake on our order and did not recitfy it (she brought out sea urchin instead of eel--when we brought it to her attention, she did not remove the unwanted, uneaten item from our bill), AND there was a long hair in one of our rolls! At most sushi establishments, they bring out the items as they are prepared, but here, we had to wait a fairly long time before  being served, and then it was everything, all at once.  Plus, i really like it when the meal commences with a nice, warm hand towel and some complimentary edaname--typical of most sushi places, but NOT here. Overall, a very unpleasant, unappetizing, unsatisfying gastronomical experience!"'}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2008-06-02 15:01:40', 'review_text': "This is a nice place to sit outside on State St.  I was a tad bit early for sushi (they don't start making sushi until 5:30), so I decided on their Warm Spinach Salad instead.  It was deeeelish.  I had a blackberry martini to sip on, which was also really good.  The server was really nice and attentive the entire time.  

I've also been here previously and have sat in their outside area upstairs, which is also nice.  

I'm curious to try their sushi soon, which might alter my rating."}]}

{'name': 'Char West', 'address': '221 Stearns Wharf', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Fish & Chips, Food, Seafood, American (Traditional), Fast Food, Coffee & Tea, Breakfast & Brunch', 'hours': {'Monday': '7:0-17:0', 'Tuesday': '7:0-17:0', 'Wednesday': '7:0-17:0', 'Thursday': '7:0-17:0', 'Friday': '7:0-17:0', 'Saturday': '7:0-19:0', 'Sunday': '7:0-19:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': False, 'validated': True, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': False, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': True, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 3.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-26 04:52:35', 'review_text': "It was the worst fish n chips I've ever had. I believe the fish was tilapia as it tasted muddy. We felt disgusted after eating there. The same type of fish was used in the fish taco. We were hungry and was super disappointed with the meal. If you want to eat muddy tasty fish, you can give it a try. It's worst than the frozen fish from the grocery store."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-09 18:16:50', 'review_text': "Nice stop on the pier for coffee

This is a no frills, no fuss, coffee shop (but also serves  food?!) right on the edge of the pier.  It looks like they are not getting extremely high marks for food, but if you go into the place it doesn't feel like a spot for a gourmet meal. What it is great for, and why I'm giving it four stars, is because of the beautiful view over the pier.  It has some awesome seating on the rail, right outside. I suggest going there early in the morning, maybe even for sunrise, and getting a coffee. I also grabbed a bagel, toasted with cream cheese. It felt like a Bagel experience you would have at Starbucks or coffee bean. 

Stop in for the coffee and the views!"}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-17 17:55:00', 'review_text': 'Absolutely my favorite spot for breakfast in Santa Barbara! Casual outdoor dining area on Stearns wharf with absolutely gorgeous view of the ocean and the hills of Santa Barbara. Francisco, Blanca and the rest of the staff are always friendly and offer excellent service. They serve a range of espresso drinks, and a nice breakfast (and lunch) menu. My personal favorite is the huevos rancheros.  A great place to eat and appreciate the beauty of Santa Barbara.'}]}

{'name': 'California Wood-Fired Catering', 'address': '', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Food Trucks, Event Planning & Services, Pizza, Restaurants, Caterers, Food', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2015-05-24 00:32:27', 'review_text': 'We had them provide pizza for about 100 folks at Municipal Wine. Food was great -- salad, pizza, and gelato. All great. 

They warned us that it would be hard to get pizzas out for that large a crowd, and they were right. But they did the best they could in the situation and everyone was happy. Their chefs worked hard to please and did a great job. 

Only negatives were: underestimated salad, so we ran out a little early. And Email response was a little slow. That said, a pleasure to work with and tasty food!'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2013-07-25 22:35:25', 'review_text': 'California Wood-Fired Catering is delicious and perfect for a casual, fun event! I have had the pleasure of working with them many times for events at the private event venue that I manage. While I have heard from a few clients that the owner can be sometimes difficult to get a hold of, I myself have never had a problem reaching him by calling the number listed on their website. Either way they always come through with the events that they book and the guests always rave about how fun it is having a wood-fired burning oven popping out fresh pizzas as well as how delicious the food is.'}, {'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2013-07-06 04:21:37', 'review_text': 'This year for 4th of July we checked out the Stow House old fashioned 4th of July:) What a pleasant surprise. We were lucky enough to stumble on these pizza people who were making pizza in special oven:) it was really good and hope they can come to our school carnivals next year:)'}]}

{'name': 'Aperitivo', 'address': '7 W Haley St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Desserts, Food, Bars, Wine Bars, Coffee & Tea, Nightlife, Tapas/Small Plates, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Wednesday': '16:30-21:0', 'Thursday': '16:30-21:0', 'Friday': '16:30-21:0', 'Saturday': '16:30-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': None, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': None, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': None}, 'business_stars': 5.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 05:03:21', 'review_text': 'I am a foodie, I travel for work and have been fortunate enough to have amazing food all over the world. That being said this is one of the most underrated restaurants in Santa Barbara I can easily say this is one of the top three restaurants in Santa Barbara.  My recommendation would to be to order anything with the burrata on it! The 24 hrs burrata, the pere brushchette , and the stratacciatella brushchette were all amazing! The passion fruit margarita is also to die f

Thank you for upping the food game in Santa Barbara Aperitivo! 

Side note, my other two favorite restaurants in Santa Barbara are the Black Sheep and Bouchon'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-13 02:30:17', 'review_text': "No hesitation here with the 5 star review! Excellent food, stellar service,  and guaranteed high quality product every time.  When I want fresh and delicious pasta, Aperativo is my go-to.  I appreciate their dedication and consistency. Highly recommend for date night since its a cozy intimate venue with an open kitchen. I'm also a big fan of Tues pasta club for take out,  excellent wine pairings every time."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-07 01:01:24', 'review_text': 'I ordered the box of wine for pick up and was not disappointed. They were all wonderful wines! I highly recommend it AND the Pasta Club. The pasta selections are very flavorful and pair wonderfully with the wine. I plan to order everytime I am in town.'}]}

{'name': 'Bettina', 'address': '1014 Coast Village Rd', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Italian, Pizza', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Tuesday': '16:0-20:30', 'Wednesday': '16:0-20:30', 'Thursday': '16:0-20:30', 'Friday': '16:0-20:30', 'Saturday': '16:0-20:30', 'Sunday': '16:0-20:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': True, 'valet': True}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': False, 'divey': False, 'intimate': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': True, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-14 02:46:25', 'review_text': 'The hype is over for this place. Local, who used to use this place for everything, and a spot to celebrate girlfriends birthdays. The food was not the issue. The staff is flat, unengaging and silent. You can feel their stuffy awkward energy. As someone who used to be a server myself, I always love being courteous to server staff/tipping well. But man, very hard to do here.'}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-10 20:40:01', 'review_text': "Omg I'm a hard core pizza aficionado and this could be my new favorite pizza place in North America. Don't let it's location in the Montecito Country Mart fool you, please make a reservation asap. 

The menu is very tight but that's fine. Everyone raves about the carbonara pizza but I hate eggs do we skipped it. We wanted a light lunch to save room for steak dinner so we opted for a bottle of Sancerre, baby gems salad and meat lovers pizza. They all hit perfectly!

The server was terrific. The ambiance felt like a garden getaway and parking was too easy. Please run to this lovely restaurant and grab a matchbox or two for the memories."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-06 05:51:02', 'review_text': "Decided to check out Bettina during our recent trip to Santa Barbara and boy was it a great experience. The location is random (in the Montecito country mart shopping center) but the inside and the courtyard of the restaurant are charming. And we figured we came to a good spot when we noticed all the locals either dining there or picking up pies. Everything we ordered was delicious! We got the burrata to start, that had this amazing green pistachio/veggie paste on top - it also came with an excellent Focaccia. Broccolini, which was tangy, charred to perfection and just delish.  And two pizzas, the mushroom and pepperoni, which may have been the best I've had. Great little spot in SB, highly recommend."}]}

{'name': 'Don Q Family Billiard Center', 'address': '1128 Chapala St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Nightlife, Pool Halls', 'hours': {'Monday': '12:0-2:0', 'Tuesday': '12:0-2:0', 'Wednesday': '12:0-2:0', 'Thursday': '12:0-2:0', 'Friday': '12:0-2:0', 'Saturday': '12:0-2:0', 'Sunday': '12:0-2:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': None, 'OutdoorSeating': False, 'WiFi': None, 'RestaurantsTakeOut': None, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': False, 'Ambience': {'divey': None, 'hipster': None, 'casual': True, 'touristy': None, 'trendy': None, 'intimate': None, 'romantic': None, 'classy': None, 'upscale': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-22 17:31:14', 'review_text': "I've been going to Don Q for 40+ years! While other pool halls have come and gone, Don Q has endured - I think they still have the same 70s-80s rock playlist in the jukebox. They have the highest quality tables and cloth, both bar and regulation size. It's fun and comfortable with the kids, a date, your wife or the guys - never feels seedy or uncomfortable. The beer and snack selection have increased greatly over time, and are downright over the top now. My only wishes: that they still had scoring beads for straight pool, some chalk cones, and didn't require the felt pad under the cue ball at break. Nonetheless, Don Q is the absolute best place to play pool in SB."}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-23 23:15:31', 'review_text': "this place is not a real billiards hall. the felt on all the pool tables is in  bad shape & when u ask the owner about it he'll just be rude.! stiix in ventura is where u have to go to play on real billiards tables. the only reason they r still open is because the kids know they can drink there !"}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2019-04-22 04:55:17', 'review_text': "The management at Don Q is probably the worst we've ever encountered in any business venue. We visited there after speaking to someone over the phone to discuss a possible opportunity for a large party event. The venue was relatively full but not overwhelming and the individual in charge couldn't take even a minute to talk to us complaining he was too busy; and, he even avoided us even though we waited for a possible 5 minutes of his time. 

Along side this extreme rudeness, the venue allows outside food to be brought in. It wreaked of uncovered food throughout the place. Food on every counter and bar stool. Quite gross. 

I have to say I will never visit Don Q's again. Management is the rudest I've ever encountered and the place smells. They have a lot to learn about running a business and they missed out on a lucrative opportunity."}]}

{'name': "Javan's", 'address': '938 Embarcadero Del Nrte', 'city': 'Goleta', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Sandwiches, Restaurants, Burgers', 'hours': None, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'classy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2014-02-25 06:54:05', 'review_text': "Sigh ... Javan's is no more :'(  I miss it already."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2013-09-10 00:43:52', 'review_text': "It perplexes me that this place is always so empty. Honestly it is the best food in IV without a doubt and it's because the owners double as the cooks and are invested in the overall quality of their ingredients and product. They are always entertaining and you could learn a thing or two from just conversing with them during your lunch. Consider helping out this humble mom and pop shop before heading to a big franchise restaurant because they do not compromise anything in their menu and are competitively priced compared to the rest of IV. 

I would recommend the Tuna sandwich for it's delicious combination of dressings and tastiness of the fish. Every bite is savory and leaves you wanting more. You can't go wrong with any of the sandwiches really though."}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2013-09-09 04:07:36', 'review_text': "The owners of this place should seriously consider investing in a good quality sign for out front.  Currently they have an unlit vinyl sign so the place is basically unnoticeable, especially at night.  I bet they would really see business improve if they weren't cheap about the sign.

Good sandwiches and chili though."}]}

{'name': 'Carrillo Dining Commons', 'address': 'Ocean Rd', 'city': 'Isla Vista', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Restaurants, Italian, Asian Fusion, Breakfast & Brunch, Delis, American (New), American (Traditional)', 'hours': {'Monday': '17:0-20:0', 'Tuesday': '17:0-20:0', 'Wednesday': '17:0-20:0', 'Thursday': '17:0-20:0', 'Friday': '17:0-20:0', 'Saturday': '17:0-20:0', 'Sunday': '17:0-20:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': None, 'street': False, 'lot': None, 'validated': None}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'free', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': False, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': False}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 3.0, 'review_date': '2021-11-21 08:42:24', 'review_text': 'Hot take but when you live in Manzi, you see the reality that Carrillo is...well. She has her good days and she certainly had her bad days. I will give them this though, their brunch on the weekends was top tier. During my CHI-5 freshman year my friends and I would commute to Carrillo for Sunday brunch (we were very late risers so it was that serious). Nothing in all of the UCSB dining halls outbeats the egg station. Chefs kiss. Anyway I appreciated their multicultural days once a quarter. Furthermore, their fruit selection was always better than Ortega and DLG. The froyo is either a hit or miss. Once they had red bean and black sesame and me and all the intl girls were here for it, but sometimes they had REDBULL flavor during midterm season...yikes...but all said, Carrillo is pretty standard.'}, {'review_stars': 1.0, 'review_date': '2021-10-13 04:30:15', 'review_text': "The food is alright.

The staff is another story. The ones who act up are sad losers with nothing else to look forward to in life but harass others for no reason. I personally had a bad experience with the staff, I do not think I am the only one who had this issue. I was walking back to the water bottle station at around the end of operating hours (no students in the building). My hands were full with empty paper plates that they make us throw away on the other side of the building and i had just finished eating, so my mask was off. Instantly after getting up and walking to the water station, two workers started yelling at me and cornered me (1-2 feet apart) into the side of the water bottle filling station. Keep in mind no one was around me besides my two other friends, they left their workstations, went across the room to yell at me.

They called me demented (while i was filling up my water bottle) said that we were in a pandemic for 18 months and that I didn't care, all the while ironically not enforcing their own rules (i have seen them without their masks multiple times). If they truly cared about the pandemic they would certainly wash the self serve handles after every use, maintain 6 feet social distance and enforce people to use hand sanitizers and wash hands. The reality is that they enjoy going out of their way to yell at students because they have sad depressing lives and have no sense of politeness or moral decency. Who calls a student demented. This isn't an isolated incident, something needs to be done about this issue."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2019-04-26 20:38:42', 'review_text': 'great burgers at the grill , and the cream cheese brownies are delicious ! also the employee at salad, the girl wearing glasses named Alex, was great at helping me , super nice, and overall made me feel welcome my first year at UCSB. i will be visiting salad again because i am vegan! glad to have that employee always helping me. the other employees are also nice but not as helpful. salad is my favorite!!'}]}

{'name': 'Trattoria Vittoria', 'address': '30 E Victoria St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Italian, Restaurants', 'hours': {'Tuesday': '17:0-21:0', 'Wednesday': '17:0-21:0', 'Thursday': '17:0-21:0', 'Friday': '17:0-22:0', 'Saturday': '17:0-22:0', 'Sunday': '17:0-21:0'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'valet': False, 'garage': None, 'street': True, 'lot': False, 'validated': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': True, 'OutdoorSeating': None, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'touristy': False, 'hipster': False, 'romantic': None, 'divey': False, 'intimate': None, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'classy': None, 'casual': None}}, 'business_stars': 4.0, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2022-01-09 04:55:39', 'review_text': "Great italian food. came here on a whim and thorough enjoyed it. will return next time i'm visiting santa barbara."}, {'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-11 08:50:25', 'review_text': "Their homemade pasta dishes, lasagna, tortellini and ravioli with a heavenly tomato sauce was definitely one of the most delicious dishes I've tried (and then I've been to Italy). The servers where so funny and genuine, too. We'll be back in SB when we get the chance!"}, {'review_stars': 4.0, 'review_date': '2021-12-08 17:23:35', 'review_text': 'We had an early dinner here. It filled up fast so if you can make reservations you should. 

We had an awesome dinner. Atmosphere was perfect.  Wine was delicious and the service was great. 

Next time I will come early and have a drink at the bar. Looked like a fun crowd. Enjoy!'}]}

{'name': "C'est Cheese", 'address': '827 Santa Barbara St', 'city': 'Santa Barbara', 'state': 'CA', 'categories': 'Specialty Food, Cheese Shops, Cafes, Restaurants, Breakfast & Brunch, Wine Bars, Sandwiches, Food, Event Planning & Services, Caterers, Bars, Nightlife', 'hours': {'Monday': '0:0-0:0', 'Saturday': '1:0-1:30'}, 'attributes': {'BusinessParking': {'garage': False, 'street': True, 'validated': False, 'lot': False, 'valet': False}, 'RestaurantsReservations': False, 'OutdoorSeating': True, 'WiFi': 'no', 'RestaurantsTakeOut': True, 'RestaurantsGoodForGroups': True, 'Music': None, 'Ambience': {'romantic': False, 'intimate': False, 'classy': False, 'hipster': False, 'divey': False, 'touristy': False, 'trendy': False, 'upscale': False, 'casual': True}}, 'business_stars': 4.5, 'review_info': [{'review_stars': 5.0, 'review_date': '2020-12-28 20:43:32', 'review_text': 'I loved this place. It is like a candy store for cheese and cured meats. We came here pre-covid and it was packed. 
